   "title": "Indices, Surds & Error Bounds",
   "content": "<p><strong>Index laws:</strong> \\(a^m \\times a^n = a^{m+n}\\), \\(a^m \\div a^n = a^{m-n}\\), \\((a^m)^n = a^{mn}\\), \\(a^{\\frac{1}{n}} = \\sqrt[n]{a}\\), \\(a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}\\).</p><p><strong>Surds:</strong> \\(\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{a} \\times \\sqrt{b}\\). Simplify by extracting the largest square factor. Rationalise by multiplying top and bottom by the surd.</p><p><strong>Bounds:</strong> If \\(x = 4.5\\) to 1 d.p., then \\(4.45 \\leq x < 4.55\\). UB and LB are half a unit either side of the rounded value.</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>Simplify \\(\\sqrt{50}\\)</strong></p><p>\\(\\sqrt{50} = \\sqrt{25 \\times 2} = 5\\sqrt{2}\\)</p>"
  },
